{'id': '2607.11651', 'categories': ['cs.RO', 'eess.SY'], 'pdf': 'https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.11651', 'abs': 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.11651', 'authors': ['Evangelos Ntouros', 'Ewoud J. J. Smeur'], 'title': 'Coordinated Incremental Trajectory Tracking of a Tailsitter Drone', 'comment': None, 'summary': 'This paper derives an analytical differential flatness transform for a tailsitter Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (UAV) under coordinated flight conditions using a simplified aerodynamic model. The proposed framework is formulated exclusively using rotation matrices, avoiding the ambiguities inherent to Euler angle representations. The method extends the applicability of an existing state-of-the-art differential flatness-based controller to flight regimes involving a significant vertical velocity component, where the previous approach becomes inapplicable. The proposed framework is validated experimentally with trajectories that highlight its advantages in these regimes.'}
