{'id': '2607.14044', 'categories': ['cs.AI'], 'pdf': 'https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.14044', 'abs': 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.14044', 'authors': ['Tam Nguyen', 'Hung Nguyen', 'Robert Ogburn'], 'title': 'AI-accelerated End-to-End Framework for Rapid Professional Upskilling', 'comment': '6 pages, 1 figure, 1 table', 'summary': "By 2030, 59 of every 100 workers will need reskilling or upskilling, yet the average time to close an enterprise skills gap grew from roughly 3 days in 2014 to 36 days in 2018. Most current frameworks accelerate single stages of upskilling programs and generally lack industry validation. We present an end-to-end framework that applies AI acceleration across five stages of knowledge acquisition, content development, content review and verification, teaching, and assessment development; with a strong focus on both production and learning efficiency. Three strong external signals validates the framework: the US National Association of State Boards of Accountancy reviewed and approved an upskilling program built on the framework for continuing-professional-education credits; 3 learners followed the program and passed the NVIDIA Certified Professional in Agentic AI exam in a significantly short amount of time, with 14 more in progress; the program's knowledge base supports complex downstream analysis such as the production of a robust 1,267 risk item dataset for managing multi-agent AI system risks."}
