{'id': '2608.04723', 'categories': ['cs.RO'], 'pdf': 'https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.04723', 'abs': 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.04723', 'authors': ['Erik Tjærand Frøland', 'Marco Job', 'Md Ether Deowan', 'Eleni Kelasidi'], 'title': 'A Vision-based Control Framework for Real-time Autonomous UUV Operations', 'comment': 'Accepted to IFAC WC 2026', 'summary': 'This paper presents a fully integrated vision-based framework for real-time and robust localization, autonomous navigation, and mapping for unmanned underwater vehicles (UUVs) in dynamic, visually challenging environments. The proposed pipeline enables both net-relative and global localization while generating continuous 3D maps of the surroundings in real-time. The framework was validated on synthetic datasets with ground truth and tested onboard an UUV during autonomous net-relative navigation experiments. Results demonstrate real-time performance and enhanced robustness, supporting vision-driven autonomous navigation and enabling the field deployment of marine robots for critical inspection and mapping tasks in complex underwater environments.'}
