{'id': '2608.07473', 'categories': ['cs.AI', 'cs.MA'], 'pdf': 'https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.07473', 'abs': 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.07473', 'authors': ['Xiang Yin', 'Tim Miller', 'Nico Potyka', 'Antonio Rago', 'Francesca Toni'], 'title': 'Towards an Argumentative Foundation for Evaluative AI', 'comment': None, 'summary': 'Evaluative AI (EAI) has been recently proposed as a way to support human decision-making, not by producing a single recommendation, but by presenting competing hypotheses together with evidence for and against each. In this position paper, we advocate (computational) argumentation as a particularly suitable paradigm to provide a formal, computable foundation for forms of EAI that are explainable and contestable, setting the ground for a long-term research agenda towards distributed and human-centred EAI systems.'}
