{'id': '2608.08122', 'categories': ['cs.AI', 'cs.DB', 'cs.LO'], 'pdf': 'https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.08122', 'abs': 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.08122', 'authors': ['Giacomo De Colle', 'Helena Blackmore', 'Chris Partridge'], 'title': 'Constraining ontology mappings using metaphysical choices', 'comment': None, 'summary': 'In this paper we discuss the foundations behind a novel methodology for the validation of semantic mappings between different data sources based upon different foundation ontologies, where the methodology builds a framework based upon the metaphysical commitments of the ontologies. We provide as example the test case of mappings between IES and BFO, and we especially focused on providing cardinality constraints on the mappings between the two ontologies. In order to demonstrate the applicability of our method, we showcased how these principles can be operationalized through SPARQL queries validating the results of a mapping pipeline.'}
