{'id': '2608.09438', 'categories': ['cs.CV'], 'pdf': 'https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.09438', 'abs': 'https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.09438', 'authors': ['Jie Zhu', 'Mingyu Ding', 'Boqiang Duan', 'Leye Wang', 'Jingdong Wang'], 'title': 'Unveiling the Secret of AdaLN-Zero in Diffusion Transformer', 'comment': 'Accept by IEEE TPAMI 2026, camera-ready version', 'summary': 'Diffusion transformer (DiT), a rapidly emerging architecture for image generation, has gained much attention. However, despite ongoing efforts to improve its performance, the understanding of DiT remains superficial. In this work, we delve into and investigate a critical conditioning mechanism within DiT, adaLN-Zero, which achieves superior performance compared to adaLN. Our work studies three potential elements driving this performance, including an SE-like structure, zero-initialization, and a "gradual" update order, among which zero-initialization is proved to be the most influential. Building on this understanding, we propose an analysis-guided initialization strategy, termed adaLN-Gaussian, which serves both as an empirical validation of our analysis and as a practical initialization method that consistently improves optimization efficiency. On the other hand, inspired by the SE-like structure, we introduce an improved conditioning mechanism called SE-adaLN-Zero. Extensive experiments following DiT on four datasets, especially on ImageNet1K demonstrate the effectiveness and generalization of adaLN-Gaussian and SE-adaLN-Zero. Beyond class-to-image generation, we also evaluate the generalization of the two improved methods on text-to-image generation.'}
